<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Valois-Angoulême</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1515">1515</a>–<a href="/years/1589">1589</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Valois-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angouleme">Angoulême</a> was a branch of the French royal Valois dynasty, descended from John, Count of Angoulême, a younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans">Louis I, Duke of Orléans</a>. Its head, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a>, succeeded his cousin Louis XII as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1515, and the line ruled France through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a> and the Wars of Religion until the death of Henry III in 1589, when the crown passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-valois-angouleme.jpg" alt="House of Valois-Angoulême" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlodangio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Philippe_de_Valois.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
